  "conclusions": [
    "Material9821 alone uses a private clone of template225/pixl227. Stock donor tags and 548 other rmsh postprocess records remain unchanged.",
    "All twelve shader variants retain every original ALU/fetch instruction byte and native routes. One KILL_GT instruction and one unused literal component implement the measured finite-alpha comparison.",
    "The new Xbox shader header/scheduling is assembled and validated with the installed Xbox360 SDK; original instruction bits are restored because the assembler text round trip normalizes unused fields.",
    "Ten dynamic-light draws executed in both comparison recordings. Original: replacement blend and ten black overwrites. Candidate35: additive blend and zero black overwrites.",
    "The witnessed c252.w threshold equals original RB_ALPHA_REF bits 0x3f008081 in all sampled passes.",
    "At (711,197), 300 final-output samples have no sub-0.2 max-RGB values in candidate35; original has ten. Minimum max-RGB rises from 0.08798 to 0.30303.",
    "Saved observer command/result and emitted camera constants match exactly. Simulated effect time is not a full restored savestate."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Only the byte-attributed model10177 mesh0 part1 sampled contribution is corrected and checked by this run. Other material users and the searchlight protrusion require separate checks.",
    "Full cutout-edge coverage, shadow/global shader paths, traversal, advertisement readability, audio, physical Xbox360 and system link are not accepted by these numeric samples.",
    "Only three of the twelve private pixel programs executed for the selected part in this recording; the others have structural/assembler validation.",
    "Finite-alpha equivalence is verified; NaN rejection differs from hardware comparison. Original texture-alpha and exposure paths are expected finite.",
    "Probe timing is not production performance. Candidate35 is an isolated candidate32-based material correction; candidate34 billboard mip correction is not included.",
    "No shared runtime, installed map or LIVE package was changed; no release promotion."
